-- title:
--   Density of the j-finite chart in a fibre
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural number $N_0 \neq 0$ and a prime $q$, and let $\kappa$ be a field of characteristic $q$ equipped with an algebra structure over the base ring `DRLevel.R q`. Write $\mathcal{O} =$ `IgusaScheme.chartAlgFin (N₀ * q) q` for the subalgebra of the field `modularFunctionFieldFull (N₀ * q)` consisting of the elements integral over the [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt q`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8)-subalgebra generated by the modular function `jFull (N₀ * q)`, and let `DRLevel.fibre (algebraMap (DRLevel.R q) κ)` be the fibre product of the structure morphism `IgusaScheme.igusaTo (N₀ * q) q` from the Igusa scheme of level $N_0q$ to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of `DRLevel.R q` along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the structure map `DRLevel.R q` $\to \kappa$. Let $c$ be a morphism from $\operatorname{Spec}(\kappa \otimes_{\mathrm{DRLevel.R}\,q} \mathcal{O})$ to this fibre such that: the composite of $c$ with the first projection equals $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the right inclusion $\mathcal{O} \to \kappa \otimes \mathcal{O}$ followed by the canonical morphism `IgusaScheme.ιFin (N₀ * q) q` of $\operatorname{Spec} \mathcal{O}$ into the Igusa scheme, and the composite of $c$ with the second projection equals $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the left inclusion $\kappa \to \kappa \otimes \mathcal{O}$. Then the range of the underlying continuous map of $c$ is dense in the fibre.
--
--   This says that the $j$-finite affine chart of the Igusa model of level $N_0q$ is topologically dense in its fibre over a characteristic-$q$ field, the complement being the finite cusp locus $j = \infty$; the proof cites the absence of isolated closed points in the fibre and the finite-type property of the two chart algebras. It is used by [`ModularCurve.DRLevel.exists_comp_pair_fibre_residueField`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRLevel.exists_comp_pair_fibre_residueField) to produce points of the fibre with prescribed residue-field data from points of the chart.
